        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-lab): keep suite HTTP probes within deadlines",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where QA suite readiness checks and image-generation polling could wait indefinitely when a local HTTP endpoint accepted a connection but stopped responding. Their polling loops had deadlines, but individual fetches could outlive those deadlines.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nLab readiness, gateway readiness, and image polling now pass the remaining operation budget into guarded fetches and clamp retry sleeps to that same deadline. The shared JSON helper also has a bounded default for callers without a phase deadline.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThere is no product runtime change. QA Lab runs now fail within their declared budgets instead of blocking later scenarios and artifact collection.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- Focused fake-timer regression coverage added for lab readiness, gateway readiness/body reads, and image polling\n- Independent autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n- Fork CI: [run 29395805097](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29395805097) passed, including all required test, type, lint, build, and CI-gate checks\n\nAI-assisted: yes. Allow edits by maintainers is enabled.\n",
